{"kind":"grammar","lang":"en","entities":{"n5-909":{"renderings":[{"id":"3a662698aee7c666","role":"label","field":"name","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-909"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Past"},{"id":"e4f23b63b696cb9f","role":"prose","field":"shortExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-909"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"The plain past of an い-adjective."},{"id":"e126c763db9f03fb","role":"prose","field":"longExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-909"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"い-adjectives carry their own tense: the past replaces い with かった. Unlike English, the adjective itself changes, not a verb."},{"id":"68655634ed69f6e6","role":"prose","field":"formation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-909"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Drop the final い and add かった: 高い -> 高かった. Irregular: いい -> よかった."},{"id":"25d0e55f4384c320","role":"label","field":"derives","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-909"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"past (かった)"}]}}}